  "name": "Brazier hall",
  "description": "The demo of the puzzle runtime (mw-e15.3): a 10 m hall whose north doorway is shut by a portcullis. Three unlit braziers stand against the walls (west, north and east); when all three burn for a second the puzzle brazier-hall is solved and the portcullis rises onto the vault corridor. Nothing says how to light them: a burning barrel waits by the south-west corner for anyone willing to carry it from brazier to brazier, a spell of fire (Ember, Firebolt) does it from across the room (the bolt lands on the wall behind a brazier and its heat reaches it), and any other flame, arrow or burning thing counts the same, because the puzzle reads what burns, not what lit it. Walking into the northern half discovers the puzzle (its discovery volume). Reach it with ?scene=brazier-hall.",
